 Only the **browse names** are configurable, not their structural position in the tree (that is hardwired in the OPC UA client). The same applies to the four storage nodes above — their fields (e.g. `StueckzahlGesamt`, `StueckzahlRot`) are hardwired in `PlcStorageGateway`, only the browse name of each parent node is adjustable. `settings_service.apply_settings()` additionally keeps an in-memory cache up to date and mirrors `polling_interval_ms` into `plc_handshake.POLL_INTERVAL_S`. Changes via `PUT /settings/` are possible at any time — except the target node of an order type while an order of that type is active (**409**); the storage nodes are not subject to this lock.
+
+## Plant time for manual orders
+
+`ORDER_PLANT_TIMEZONE` defaults to `Europe/Berlin`. The backend supplies local date/time suggestions; `Startzeit` is sent without a timezone offset. The existing `pytz` package supplies timezone data in the Alpine image. These fields do not introduce additional scheduling.
+
+## Product catalog mirror
+
+`PRODUCT_CATALOG_REFRESH_INTERVAL_S=30` controls the background read interval; `PRODUCT_CATALOG_STALE_AFTER_S=300` controls catalog freshness independently of live order status. Values must be finite, positive and the stale limit greater than the refresh interval. A read failure blocks first admission immediately; stored data remain intact until a successful sync. Apply migration `plc_catalog_01` first. `python -m app.scripts.sync_product_catalog` imports once without starting the order worker.
