 ## Areas without independent test coverage
 
 `backend/tests/` covers the order pipeline, the PLC handshake, settings, and the storage consumer very broadly (see [Development and Tests](Development-and-Tests-English)). `analytics.py`/`analytics_router.py`, as well as the review path in `orders_router.py`, have **no dedicated** test file — only incidental coverage via other tests. Implemented as current behavior, but with less test coverage than the rest of the pipeline.
+
+## Entry preparation and admission reconciliation (Issue #30)
+
+`GET /orders/input-context?order_type=production` or `delivery` returns availability, independent unused ID/PLC-number suggestions, plant-local date/time, validated products, observed slot capacity, timestamps, errors and refresh intervals. Reading does not reserve identifiers.
+
+Both existing POST routes retain `OrderPayload`. First admission validates fresh product data, ID/text pairs, capacity, strict integer PLC values, offset-free time, SIMATIC DATE bounds and serial-range overflow. Existing identical orders are resolved before catalog checks; conflicting content remains `409`. Field-specific validation returns structured `422` details.
+
+Type-specific detail now returns `OrderDetailView` with the complete normalized `mes_auftrag` and refresh intervals; list DTOs stay unchanged. The immutable input supports reconciliation after a timeout or proxy-503. The catalog contract is live-verified; first admission uses the persisted mirror and rejects unavailable prerequisites.
+
+`POST /orders/catalog/sync?order_type=production|delivery` reads the PLC and updates the catalog tables only. `plc_catalog_product` stores ID/text/index/specification/availability/time; `plc_catalog_state` stores per-type capacity and success/error status. Run migration `plc_catalog_01` before using the application. Existing order and article data are unchanged.
